    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `riskFlag` is a derived, read-only response field on `Owner`, computed the same way the codebase already computes `ownerSegment`, `membershipLevel`, etc. \u2014 via a MapStruct expression in `OwnerMapper` calling a small helper. Four edits:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (readOnly), so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it.\n\n2. **`RiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 `RiskFlag.of(owner)` returns `true` when **any** of the three signals holds:\n   - **possible duplicate** \u2192 `owner.getPossibleDuplicate()` (set by the existing `FlagPossibleDuplicate` step)\n   - **disposable-adjacent email** \u2192 `OwnerEmail.isDisposableAdjacent(owner.getEmail())`\n   - **city over soft capacity** \u2192 `owner.getCapacityWarning()` (set by the existing `FlagCapacityWarning` step, the 40\u201349 approaching-capacity band below the hard limit of 50)\n\n3. **`OwnerEmail.java`** \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacent(email)`. Since the exact disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) are already *rejected* at create time and never reach storage, \"adjacent\" is defined as resembling one without being one: a subdomain of a disposable domain (`inbox.mailinator.com`), or carrying the same provider brand under a different name (`mailinator.net`, `tempmail.io`). Null/blank/unrelated \u2192 false.\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 wired the `riskFlag` mapping.\n\nReusing the stored `possibleDuplicate` and `capacityWarning` flags keeps `riskFlag` consistent with the other derived DTO fields (all computed from stored owner state at response time). A normal owner (no duplicate, no email, unique city) yields `false`, satisfying `coreRiskFlagFalseNormally`.",
